WEBVTT

00:04.371 --> 00:08.171
We've completely failed to
stop them at the battlefront.

00:08.409 --> 00:11.378
But the individual squadrons
are doing all right.

00:11.712 --> 00:13.077
Well, yes.

00:13.247 --> 00:16.148
But you haven't reduced
the enemy numbers much.

00:16.350 --> 00:18.052
Don't be so detached about this.

00:18.052 --> 00:20.384
You're involved
in this plan as well.

00:20.587 --> 00:22.222
Calm down, Nereis.

00:22.222 --> 00:24.952
I know. This is our plan.

00:25.125 --> 00:26.727
Besides, how could we have predicted...

00:26.727 --> 00:29.491
...that their mine attacks would
have gone on so long?

00:30.097 --> 00:30.831
Because of that...

00:30.831 --> 00:34.234
...our fleet was not in
the best shape to fight...

00:34.234 --> 00:36.065
...when the enemy ships arrived.

00:46.046 --> 00:47.982
The fact that our flagship
needs to take part...

00:47.982 --> 00:49.609
...means things aren't
looking good.

00:50.451 --> 00:52.112
What do we do next, Nereis?

00:52.519 --> 00:55.545
I guess we can't retreat now, can we?

00:56.123 --> 00:57.351
Of course not.

00:57.558 --> 01:00.361
Our forces now completely
surround the Aptic Gate.

01:00.361 --> 01:02.921
Thanks to that, we're managing
to hold them off at the front.

01:06.266 --> 01:10.896
If we retreat, that would give
the enemy time to remobilize.

01:11.672 --> 01:14.140
And if that happened,
we'd simply be wiped out.

01:15.242 --> 01:17.244
Do you want us
to just sit here and wait...

01:17.244 --> 01:21.340
...while the enemy goes ahead
and destroys us, Nefee?

01:22.249 --> 01:25.707
I was hoping for some evidence
of Spectacular Insanity here.

01:27.955 --> 01:31.288
Sorry to disappoint you, but you
won't find any insanity in me.

01:32.059 --> 01:33.321
Where do you think you're going?

01:34.461 --> 01:35.826
I'm taking a bath.

01:36.096 --> 01:37.063
A bath?

01:37.798 --> 01:40.000
I'm going to have a bath.

01:40.000 --> 01:41.835
I'm feeling a bit sticky.

01:41.835 --> 01:45.105
It's not good for the commander
to be suffering from exhaustion.

01:45.105 --> 01:47.767
I must get my rest when I can.

01:48.175 --> 01:50.336
Well, I suppose so.

01:50.644 --> 01:53.875
You should take some time out
and get a bit of rest as well.

01:54.114 --> 01:56.517
Hey, you understand
the situation here?

01:56.517 --> 01:58.585
We're in the middle of a battle.

01:58.585 --> 02:00.754
This ship could be destroyed
at any time!

02:00.754 --> 02:03.490
Being killed in action
while taking a bath...

02:03.490 --> 02:05.822
...seems quite silly
to say the least, Nereis!

02:07.294 --> 02:10.998
It would be a great dishonor to
know that I'd let my men die in vain.

02:10.998 --> 02:14.058
At the very least I would like
to choose where I end my life.

02:20.574 --> 02:23.600
So, a bathtub is your choice
of a suitable place to die?

02:30.551 --> 02:34.248
The Battle for Aptic Gate Begins

02:39.760 --> 02:44.595
Banner of the Stars

04:14.655 --> 04:15.849
You going to fire at me?!

04:16.623 --> 04:18.955
All personnel! Brace for attack!

04:28.569 --> 04:30.270
There's no response
from the laser cannon!

04:30.270 --> 04:33.173
There have been breaches in
the hull from Sectors 3 to 17...

04:33.173 --> 04:35.008
...and the first passageway
has also lost pressure!

04:35.008 --> 04:38.145
Multiple damages. Three crew
dead and another five wounded!

04:38.145 --> 04:40.380
Temperature rising sharply!

04:40.380 --> 04:42.683
The armor will melt at this rate!

04:42.683 --> 04:44.583
Request permission
to jettison the armor!

04:46.053 --> 04:48.188
Explosion in Sector 23!

04:48.188 --> 04:50.490
The automatic fire extinguishing
system has failed!

04:50.490 --> 04:51.692
It's looking bad.

04:51.692 --> 04:52.852
Lafiel!

04:54.561 --> 04:56.763
Rescue the crew members!
And hurry it up!

04:56.763 --> 04:59.299
Permission granted to take
any action necessary!

04:59.299 --> 05:01.699
Do whatever you have to do.

05:02.169 --> 05:03.670
I appreciate that, but...

05:03.670 --> 05:06.036
...I don't know how much
we can do now!

05:06.240 --> 05:07.908
Deca-Commander Abriel!

05:07.908 --> 05:09.375
What's your current situation?

05:11.845 --> 05:15.115
Request permission to withdraw
from the front, Unit Commander.

05:15.115 --> 05:17.276
Permission granted, Basroil.

05:18.318 --> 05:20.878
It's unfortunate,
but it can't be helped.

05:21.955 --> 05:23.388
It's very unfortunate.

05:25.058 --> 05:27.027
Line Wing Aviator,
can we save the ship?

05:27.027 --> 05:28.562
It's almost impossible.

05:28.562 --> 05:31.465
We're barely holding on.

05:31.465 --> 05:33.033
If we jettison the
anti-matter fuel...

05:33.033 --> 05:34.668
...we can perhaps save the vessel...

05:34.668 --> 05:36.103
...but it can't be done automatically.

05:36.103 --> 05:38.663
And we're really short
on people here.

05:39.873 --> 05:41.864
Damn, why did we have to lose him?

05:44.444 --> 05:45.843
I'm left with no choice.

05:46.880 --> 05:48.404
All crew! Abandon ship!

05:49.249 --> 05:50.417
Is the Calike still
in working order?

05:50.417 --> 05:51.577
No damage.

05:51.752 --> 05:52.819
Senior Aviator...

05:52.819 --> 05:55.622
...get the Calike prepared
immediately for departure!

05:55.622 --> 05:56.680
Yes, Captain!

05:57.057 --> 05:59.326
Supply Officer, get the crew
onto the Calike.

05:59.326 --> 06:00.258
Yes, Captain!

06:05.432 --> 06:07.161
This is something...

06:08.035 --> 06:09.969
...I never thought I'd have to do.

06:17.477 --> 06:19.707
All crew! This is the captain!

06:20.047 --> 06:22.516
You are temporarily discharged
from your responsibilities.

06:22.516 --> 06:24.584
Abandon your posts immediately...

06:24.584 --> 06:26.586
...and move quickly
to the Calike deck.

06:26.586 --> 06:27.484
I repeat!

06:27.821 --> 06:30.257
You are temporarily discharged
from your responsibilities.

06:30.257 --> 06:30.757
Abandon your posts immediately...

06:30.757 --> 06:32.959
- Ekuryua...
- Abandon your posts immediately...

06:32.959 --> 06:34.187
- Can you deal with my cat?
...and move quickly
to the Calike deck.

06:34.861 --> 06:37.591
He's in my room. I've already
put him in his travel carrier.

06:43.136 --> 06:44.194
That's a relief!

06:47.808 --> 06:50.174
I'll go and prepare the Calike
for boarding now.

06:51.378 --> 06:54.548
I don't think there's much
more for me to do up here.

06:54.548 --> 06:57.684
Do you mind if I go and give
Supply Officer Lin a hand?

06:57.684 --> 07:00.354
After all, the ones injured
are my subordinates.

07:00.354 --> 07:03.290
As I said before, just do
whatever you have to do.

07:03.290 --> 07:04.723
That's right.

07:04.991 --> 07:06.390
Right, then. I'll head down.

07:10.864 --> 07:12.165
Basroil...

07:12.165 --> 07:13.598
You had a short life.

07:14.101 --> 07:14.795
Forgive me.

07:23.243 --> 07:26.906
It's obvious that we don't
have very much time left.

07:41.828 --> 07:45.265
Enemy attack to the right!
Watch out behind you!

07:45.265 --> 07:47.667
Keep firing! Get that one!
Turn the ship around!

07:47.667 --> 07:49.436
Got him!
Now come around!

07:49.436 --> 07:50.771
Prepare the laser cannon!

07:50.771 --> 07:53.205
Guard ship unit destroyed!

07:55.142 --> 07:56.676
How bad are the losses?

07:56.676 --> 07:58.644
Over forty-five percent, sir.

08:01.014 --> 08:03.107
So, this is it.

08:03.316 --> 08:04.476
This is what it's come to.

08:08.155 --> 08:10.123
We're going to cover the rear.

08:10.123 --> 08:12.125
Send the Neeroil out in front!

08:12.125 --> 08:12.692
Captain!

08:12.692 --> 08:14.353
The enemy fleet is retreating!

08:19.132 --> 08:21.862
Hmm. That was faster than expected.

08:22.335 --> 08:24.803
The main fleet commanded
by His Highness.

08:30.744 --> 08:34.942
The enemy around the Aptic Gate
has made a clear move.

08:36.516 --> 08:39.212
So, they finally gave up
the struggle?

08:39.653 --> 08:43.953
The enemy will be forced to fight
us in a decisive battle in the Aptic.

08:44.691 --> 08:48.457
That's not to say that we
have the advantage.

08:49.463 --> 08:51.798
If the current battle is a draw...

08:51.798 --> 08:53.959
...it's a strategic blow
to the Empire.

08:54.267 --> 08:55.495
We have to avoid that.

08:56.336 --> 08:57.504
Well, well.

08:57.504 --> 08:59.062
Would you look at that?

08:59.372 --> 09:01.465
Is there something wrong,
Your Highness?

09:01.741 --> 09:04.611
Can you see the formation
the enemy is moving into?

09:04.611 --> 09:06.413
This is their challenge to us.

09:06.413 --> 09:08.381
Don't you think so?

09:09.249 --> 09:10.784
I don't think so.

09:10.784 --> 09:13.119
They're just choosing
the fastest way out of there.

09:13.119 --> 09:15.519
Straight down the middle, huh?

09:15.722 --> 09:18.225
If we were to simply
let them pass through...

09:18.225 --> 09:20.026
...our losses would be
kept to a minimum.

09:20.026 --> 09:23.864
We could withdraw our fleet
from the area altogether.

09:23.864 --> 09:25.799
Thus avoiding the need to fight...

09:25.799 --> 09:28.859
...and Aptic would still remain
in the hands of the Empire.

09:29.135 --> 09:32.127
That way we could also
keep Mystel in the Empire.

09:32.506 --> 09:34.875
Is that what you're
planning to do?

09:34.875 --> 09:36.276
Of course not.

09:36.276 --> 09:38.545
You forget that I am an Abriel.

09:38.545 --> 09:41.414
After assembling
such a large fleet...

09:41.414 --> 09:43.950
...winning control of a couple
of remote planetary systems...

09:43.950 --> 09:45.679
...isn't my idea of success.

09:46.186 --> 09:48.355
The enemy has given us
the choice...

09:48.355 --> 09:50.789
...to fight or not to fight.

09:51.625 --> 09:53.226
You don't know that for sure.

09:53.226 --> 09:55.495
That may be so...

09:55.495 --> 09:59.332
...but it's clear that
the ball is in our court.

09:59.332 --> 10:01.468
We're going to have our big battle.
All right?

10:01.468 --> 10:04.869
I suppose if I disagree with you,
you'll fire me on the spot?

10:05.071 --> 10:06.606
Certainly not.

10:06.606 --> 10:09.042
You're a most competent
chief of staff.

10:09.042 --> 10:11.144
I can't dismiss you.

10:11.144 --> 10:14.614
But it may mean that I'll
no longer listen to you.

10:14.614 --> 10:16.883
I thought you might say that.

10:16.883 --> 10:19.419
I have no intention of
disagreeing with you.

10:19.419 --> 10:20.687
Like you said...

10:20.687 --> 10:24.248
...we've come this far to
eliminate the enemy fleet.

10:25.292 --> 10:26.486
Very well.

10:26.726 --> 10:29.262
The Third Fleet will maintain
its present position.

10:29.262 --> 10:32.465
We'll have the Second and Fourth
Fleets get into a cluster formation...

10:32.465 --> 10:36.060
...and attack the enemy from
the flank or from the rear.

10:36.403 --> 10:39.065
We'll position the
First Fleet out in front.

10:39.372 --> 10:41.374
The guard ships will stand by...

10:41.374 --> 10:43.740
...ready to respond
to enemy retaliation.

10:44.511 --> 10:45.712
A rough plan.

10:45.712 --> 10:48.949
But until we see how
the enemy organizes, it's a start.

10:48.949 --> 10:51.850
I'd like you to study the
efficacy of this battle strategy.

10:52.586 --> 10:53.712
Yes, sir.

10:55.188 --> 10:56.314
By the way...

10:56.590 --> 10:59.388
...there was one thing
I wanted you to tell me.

11:00.327 --> 11:01.595
Yes?

11:01.595 --> 11:04.764
Which one of the brothers did
you have a relationship with?

11:04.764 --> 11:06.333
Was it Nereis?

11:06.333 --> 11:07.766
Or was it Nefee?

11:09.135 --> 11:10.403
Commander!

11:10.403 --> 11:12.701
The First Fleet has
completed its deployment.

11:13.373 --> 11:16.409
Thank you for your effort.

11:16.409 --> 11:18.809
Distance to the enemy frontline
is 120.

11:19.212 --> 11:20.770
They're in an
oval-shaped formation...

11:21.014 --> 11:22.811
...and all ships are facing
in this direction.

11:23.316 --> 11:25.652
Their patrol ships appear
to be battle-ready...

11:25.652 --> 11:28.348
...as well as shielding
the ships inside the oval.

11:29.155 --> 11:31.224
Our primary task will be...

11:31.224 --> 11:33.927
...to break through that shell
in order to expose...

11:33.927 --> 11:35.729
...and destroy the weaker ships if...

11:35.729 --> 11:36.596
No, no.

11:36.596 --> 11:39.326
Where's the elegance in that?

11:40.867 --> 11:42.969
It may come as a surprise to you...

11:42.969 --> 11:46.106
...but I quite enjoy bullying
the weaker ones.

11:46.106 --> 11:48.540
No surprise to me.

11:49.109 --> 11:52.379
Trampling over beat up
assault vessels...

11:52.379 --> 11:54.547
...and annihilating
defenseless ships...

11:54.547 --> 11:56.616
...can be a quite a beautiful thing.

11:56.616 --> 11:58.447
Don't you agree?

11:58.785 --> 12:01.754
I think that's simply
a matter of taste.

12:02.188 --> 12:03.857
Well, my dear Chief of Staff...

12:03.857 --> 12:06.559
...there's nothing in this galaxy
that's more important...

12:06.559 --> 12:07.992
...than my taste.

12:08.061 --> 12:10.597
The commander's got to be joking.

12:10.597 --> 12:12.360
I sure hope she's joking.

12:12.832 --> 12:16.036
That and having twenty-five
patrol ship squadrons assembled...

12:16.036 --> 12:18.630
...to fight to the bitter end
using only brute force.

12:19.205 --> 12:22.936
But what other approaches
can we take?

12:23.209 --> 12:26.372
If it were up to me, I'd avoid
the battlefield altogether.

12:26.880 --> 12:28.643
And hide in Aptic.

12:29.282 --> 12:32.649
But surely that means we won't
be able to fight in the big battle?

12:33.153 --> 12:35.188
It's not an ideal situation.

12:35.188 --> 12:37.656
But it's got to be better
than the alternative.

12:38.758 --> 12:39.656
I suppose.

12:39.993 --> 12:41.261
Well...

12:41.261 --> 12:45.098
...I suppose there's no point
grumbling about this.

12:45.098 --> 12:46.433
Chief of Staff.

12:46.433 --> 12:48.568
Here's an order to all units
under my command.

12:48.568 --> 12:50.370
Separate from the supply forces...

12:50.370 --> 12:52.505
...and advance with
surveillance troops only.

12:52.505 --> 12:55.075
Ships are to prepare for
battle in regular space.

12:55.075 --> 12:57.677
We'll enter the space-time
bubbles in small groups.

12:57.677 --> 13:00.213
The squadrons Kuryudas,
Biruka, Kengafu...

13:00.213 --> 13:02.248
...Goshitol, Ferutoni, Saidoo...

13:02.248 --> 13:04.317
...and Torarisuto will...

13:04.317 --> 13:07.878
...stop the enemy from advancing
further. This is their top priority.

13:08.321 --> 13:10.983
The remainder shall focus on
penetrating the enemy fleet.

13:11.224 --> 13:13.993
They are to avoid engaging in
battle with enemy patrol ships.

13:13.993 --> 13:16.723
Even if provoked, they should not
retaliate immediately.

13:17.097 --> 13:19.899
If they enter space-time bubbles,
they'll obviously fight hard...

13:19.899 --> 13:22.602
...until they've returned
to their own ranks.

13:22.602 --> 13:24.771
We break through the outer shell
of patrol ships...

13:24.771 --> 13:27.137
...and cut deep into enemy lines.

13:27.674 --> 13:30.700
She plans to demoralize them
no matter what it takes.

13:30.944 --> 13:34.107
The signal will be when our
space-time bubble moves forward.

13:34.414 --> 13:35.210
Got that?

13:36.049 --> 13:36.947
Understood, ma'am!

13:37.550 --> 13:39.916
I will relay the order
immediately to all ships.

13:44.124 --> 13:47.389
The rearward Saidoo has
commenced space-time fusion!

13:48.228 --> 13:49.855
Inform the captain!

13:50.630 --> 13:52.699
The space-time bubble
is totally mobile...

13:52.699 --> 13:54.360
...on a course of 010.

13:56.603 --> 13:58.332
I'm not sure I feel up to this.

13:58.972 --> 14:01.338
The First Fleet has
begun to advance.

14:01.641 --> 14:04.439
In that case, we should
start our advance as well.

14:05.178 --> 14:06.813
All squadrons on the frontline...

14:06.813 --> 14:08.804
...shall launch their mobile
space-time mines.

14:21.094 --> 14:23.396
First wave.
Space-time separation!

14:23.396 --> 14:25.421
Second wave.
Space-time separation!

14:25.665 --> 14:27.496
Third wave.
Space-time separation!

14:28.434 --> 14:30.303
Our Fleet has begun its mine attack!

14:30.303 --> 14:32.505
Enemy guard ship
space-time bubbles...

14:32.505 --> 14:33.767
...have begun to retreat!

14:43.516 --> 14:46.152
Distance to enemy fleet is...

14:46.152 --> 14:50.523
...ten... nine... eight... seven...

14:50.523 --> 14:54.828
...six... five... four... three...

14:54.828 --> 14:57.023
...two... one!

14:57.297 --> 14:58.389
We've made contact!

14:59.566 --> 15:03.024
I can almost hear the
sound of scraping metal.

15:07.740 --> 15:11.369
The sound of my dear ships
being damaged.

15:12.679 --> 15:15.815
The sound of my precious men dying.

15:15.815 --> 15:17.908
It's not a sound I could ever enjoy.

15:18.318 --> 15:20.445
You might have to get used to it.

15:20.854 --> 15:21.888
How true.

15:21.888 --> 15:23.719
A pertinent observation.

15:24.290 --> 15:25.291
Sector 10 damaged!

15:25.291 --> 15:27.093
There's a break in the armor!

15:27.093 --> 15:29.459
The armor is in danger of melting!

15:31.598 --> 15:33.566
There is a danger the
ship will break apart!

15:47.280 --> 15:50.306
We've penetrated the frontline
of enemy patrol ships!

15:51.918 --> 15:53.019
Notify headquarters!

15:53.019 --> 15:55.146
And inform Futune
and Skuni as well!

15:55.822 --> 15:58.052
All ships prepare to launch
another mine attack!

15:58.491 --> 16:00.356
She looks so happy about this.

16:00.693 --> 16:02.562
Once mines are deployed...

16:02.562 --> 16:04.894
...all ships must separate into
individual space-time bubbles!

16:05.198 --> 16:07.063
All mines ready to be launched!

16:07.500 --> 16:09.024
Fire all mines!

16:15.675 --> 16:17.643
All mines have been
successfully launched!

16:18.044 --> 16:20.569
Mobilize individual
space-time bubbles!

16:21.047 --> 16:22.514
Go out there!

16:40.500 --> 16:41.990
Everyone on board?

16:43.403 --> 16:46.339
Well, we're still waiting
for Second Aviator Ekuryua and...

16:46.339 --> 16:47.440
She hasn't arrived yet?

16:47.440 --> 16:51.010
She's been delayed because
she had to retrieve Diaho.

16:51.010 --> 16:52.845
At least we know where she is.

16:52.845 --> 16:55.448
She should be here any moment, but...

16:55.448 --> 16:56.676
But what?

16:57.283 --> 17:00.453
We had to leave Paveryua
behind because of his injuries.

17:00.453 --> 17:03.389
Supply Officer Lin went
to rescue him...

17:03.389 --> 17:05.755
...but we think he might've
been in an accident.

17:06.225 --> 17:07.961
His helmet has malfunctioned...

17:07.961 --> 17:09.896
...so we can't tell
what his situation is.

17:09.896 --> 17:12.558
He's probably near Sector 1.

17:13.032 --> 17:14.829
That is, if he's still alive.

17:15.935 --> 17:17.637
What about Paveryua?

17:17.637 --> 17:20.573
We think he escaped using
one of the emergency pods.

17:20.573 --> 17:21.607
Okay.

17:21.607 --> 17:23.509
I'm going back to rescue
Supply Officer Lin.

17:23.509 --> 17:27.070
Take command of the Calike
and try to pick up Paveryua.

17:27.780 --> 17:28.781
But...

17:28.781 --> 17:30.248
That's an order, Senior Aviator!

17:35.355 --> 17:36.515
Look after that.

17:38.925 --> 17:40.449
I've got no choice.

17:41.828 --> 17:42.895
Your Highness...

17:42.895 --> 17:45.131
...you have been a great
and courageous captain.

17:45.131 --> 17:48.735
I want you to know that.

17:48.735 --> 17:52.102
I appreciate that.
I'll now leave my crew with you.

17:52.438 --> 17:53.639
Of course.

17:53.639 --> 17:55.875
They are my crew as well.

17:55.875 --> 17:56.534
Captain!

17:56.976 --> 17:58.644
We've only got five minutes!

17:58.644 --> 18:01.374
The ship could explode
at any time.

18:01.748 --> 18:04.376
If you still haven't found
the boy after five minutes...

18:04.951 --> 18:06.052
I know it's difficult...

18:06.052 --> 18:07.420
...but we'll have to give up.

18:07.420 --> 18:08.821
Please be careful.

18:08.821 --> 18:10.823
I don't want to be known as...

18:10.823 --> 18:13.693
...the senior aviator who abandoned
her captain during her first battle.

18:13.693 --> 18:14.927
Of course.

18:14.927 --> 18:17.293
I have no intention of dying here.

18:19.766 --> 18:22.200
Remember to pick up
our pods once we're out.

18:22.702 --> 18:24.533
We'll be there for you!

18:26.039 --> 18:27.233
Senior Aviator!

18:27.874 --> 18:29.136
We've got a problem.

18:29.776 --> 18:32.176
I can't get any more output
from the engine in the Calike!

18:33.012 --> 18:34.013
We can't get out of here?!

18:34.013 --> 18:35.915
We're battling against the clock!

18:35.915 --> 18:37.817
We've got to do something
before she blows!

18:37.817 --> 18:39.419
Let me come and help!

18:39.419 --> 18:40.511
Please!

18:47.927 --> 18:50.361
Wh-what happened to me...?

18:54.467 --> 18:56.435
Paveryua, where are you?!

19:01.140 --> 19:03.876
The emergency pod's been used.

19:03.876 --> 19:05.639
That must mean he
got out of here.

19:06.846 --> 19:08.006
Thank goodness!

19:19.358 --> 19:20.518
That was close.

19:21.527 --> 19:23.963
So I was out for about five minutes.

19:23.963 --> 19:27.364
But that five minutes
may have cost me my life.

19:27.900 --> 19:30.603
How typical of me.

19:30.603 --> 19:33.936
I try to act the hero
but it's all in vain.

19:35.074 --> 19:37.907
I suppose I shouldn't do things
I'm not used to.

19:38.277 --> 19:39.479
There're no emergency pods.

19:39.479 --> 19:40.913
No more pressure helmets.

19:40.913 --> 19:44.584
The pressure in the next sector
is probably five thousand daj.

19:44.584 --> 19:46.745
And the ship is about to explode.

19:49.522 --> 19:51.990
There's one thing left that I can do.

19:53.292 --> 19:55.328
But if I call for help...

19:55.328 --> 19:57.853
...I'm just going to end up
risking someone else's life.

20:41.440 --> 20:42.575
Are you all right, Jinto?

20:42.575 --> 20:45.278
I was okay until just now.

20:45.278 --> 20:47.405
But I can't say for sure anymore.

20:48.147 --> 20:50.750
You fool. Would you
have preferred that I didn't come?

20:50.750 --> 20:51.682
Of course not.

20:52.151 --> 20:54.346
Thank you. If you hadn't come,
I'd be dead.

20:54.954 --> 20:56.785
Hurry up. We don't have time.

20:59.592 --> 21:02.862
What is it with you and your
fascination with vacuums?

21:02.862 --> 21:04.230
Give me a break.

21:04.230 --> 21:05.631
I hate vacuums.

21:05.631 --> 21:08.701
I mean, Landers like me...

21:08.701 --> 21:11.704
...have this idea that vacuums
aren't very good for you.

21:11.704 --> 21:14.036
Maybe that's just superstition.

21:25.985 --> 21:30.422
Let's hurry. There should
be an emergency pod up ahead.

21:33.593 --> 21:34.753
I'm sorry.

21:34.994 --> 21:36.329
You once said...

21:36.329 --> 21:39.732
...that you didn't think
anyone would miss you...

21:39.732 --> 21:42.735
...or grieve over your passing.

21:42.735 --> 21:44.600
What? Yeah...

22:04.423 --> 22:05.324
Got it!

22:05.324 --> 22:05.983
Let's go!

22:14.800 --> 22:17.132
It's okay! Let's get out of here!

22:21.307 --> 22:23.468
What's happened to the captain
and Supply Officer Lin?

22:35.354 --> 22:37.185
Captain! Supply Officer!

22:41.861 --> 22:46.866
10:26

22:46.866 --> 22:52.827
Assault Vessel Basroil Destroyed

22:54.273 --> 22:57.834
kizukanai koto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.278 --> 23:02.941
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.717 --> 23:08.278
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.622 --> 23:13.388
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.559 --> 23:15.828
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.828 --> 23:19.025
haritsumeta kimochi ga
This tense feeling

23:21.033 --> 23:26.339
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keep facing forward

23:26.339 --> 23:29.365
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:30.276 --> 23:33.677
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.714 --> 23:39.185
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:39.185 --> 23:46.459
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.459 --> 23:51.630
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.630 --> 23:59.628
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.274 --> 24:07.446
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.446 --> 24:12.485
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our linked hands and our finger tips

24:12.485 --> 24:20.551
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.427 --> 24:25.557
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:32.171 --> 24:37.165
O Stars, listen to our plea
as our lives are but short.

24:37.376 --> 24:38.711
Our wish...

24:38.711 --> 24:42.647
...is that you will guide us to you
when we meet our end.

24:43.616 --> 24:44.850
It's strange.

24:44.850 --> 24:48.581
It almost feels like
nothing matters anymore.

24:49.188 --> 24:52.419
Maybe it's because I'm with you.

24:52.792 --> 24:53.850
You fool.

24:54.560 --> 24:57.863
I wonder who...

24:57.863 --> 24:58.264
Next Episode...
The Shapes of Bonds

24:58.264 --> 25:00.433
Next Episode...
The Shapes of Bonds
...I really am.

25:00.433 --> 25:00.797
Next Episode...
The Shapes of Bonds
